      "text": "3744.\n</answer>.<|User|>Okay, I understand the step-by-step process now. Can you also show me how to solve this using the distributive property of multiplication over addition? I think it might help me grasp the concept better. Please reason step by step.. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition can simplify the multiplication process. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can apply this property to break down the multiplication of 56 and 49 into more manageable parts.\n\nLet's rewrite 49 as \\(50 - 1\\). This way, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[ 56 \\times 49 = 56 \\times (50 - 1) \\]\n\nNow, apply the distributive property:\n\\[ 56 \\times (50 - 1) = 56 \\times 50 - 56 \\times 1 \\]\n\nLet's solve each part separately:\n1. Calculate \\(56 \\times 50\\):\n\\[ 56 \\times 50 = 56 \\times (5 \\times 10) = (56 \\times 5) \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ 56 \\times 5 = 280 \\]\n\\[ 280 \\times 10 = 2800 \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(56 \\times 1\\):\n\\[ 56 \\times 1 = 56 \\]\n\nNow, subtract the second result from the first:\n\\[ 2800 - 56 = 2744 \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 56 and 49 is:\n\\[ 56 \\times 49 = 2744 \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2744} \\]\n</answer>",
