-+\n   ```\n\n2. **Place the digits in the grid:**\n   - Place the digits of 621 along the top of the grid and the digits of 85 along the left side of the grid.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 6 | 2 | 1 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 8 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply each digit:**\n   - Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the left column and place the result in the corresponding cell of the grid. Write the tens digit in the top triangle and the units digit in the bottom triangle.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 6 | 2 | 1 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 8 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 48 | 10 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 16 | 10 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n4. **Add the diagonals:**\n   - Add the numbers in each diagonal, starting from the bottom right.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 48 | 10 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 16 | 10 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n5. **Combine the results:**\n   - The numbers along the left and bottom edges of the grid, read from top to bottom and left to right, give the final product.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 48 | 10 | 5 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n   Reading from top to bottom and left to right, we get 52785.\n\nSo, the final product of \\(621 \\times 85\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{52785}\n\\]\n\nThis method provides a visual and systematic way to perform the multiplication, making it easier to manage and understand. <|User|>Thank you for walking me through the lattice method for multiplying 621 by 85. It's clear now.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nYou're welcome! I'm glad you found the lattice method explanation clear. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any mathematical concept, feel free to ask. Understanding these methods will definitely help you tackle more complex problems with confidence. <|User|>Can you provide an example of multiplying a three-digit number by a two-digit number using the standard algorithm, but this time let's use 743 by 92?\n<\uff5cAssistant\