g place values.\n\n   - Top-left rectangle: \\(700 \\times 90 = 63000\\)\n   - Top-middle rectangle: \\(700 \\times 2 = 1400\\)\n   - Top-right rectangle: \\(40 \\times 90 = 3600\\)\n   - Middle-left rectangle: \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n   - Middle-middle rectangle: \\(40 \\times 90 = 3600\\)\n   - Middle-right rectangle: \\(3 \\times 90 = 270\\)\n   - Bottom-left rectangle: \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\)\n   - Bottom-middle rectangle: \\(3 \\times 90 = 270\\)\n   - Bottom-right rectangle: \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\)\n\n4. **Add the areas of all the smaller rectangles:**\n   \\[\n   63000 + 1400 + 3600 + 80 + 3600 + 270 + 6 + 270 + 6 = 68356\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final product of \\(743 \\times 92\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{68356}\n\\]\n\nThis method breaks down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts and helps ensure that all parts of the numbers are considered. <|User|>That's a great explanation. Can you show me how to multiply 743 by 92 using the lattice method?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.\nCertainly! Let's use the lattice method to multiply 743 by 92.\n\n1. **Set up the lattice grid:**\n   - Draw a 2x2 grid because we are multiplying a 3-digit number by a 2-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the digits of 743 and the left column with the digits of 92.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   |   |   |   |\n   +---+---+---+\n   |   |   |   |\n   +---+---+---+\n   |   |   |   |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n2. **Place the digits in the grid:**\n   - Place the digits of 743 along the top of the grid and the digits of 92 along the left side of the grid.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 7 | 4 | 3 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 9 | 2 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply each digit:**\n   - Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the left column and place the result in the corresponding cell of the grid. Write the tens digit in the top triangle and the units digit in the bottom triangle.\n\n   ```\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 7 | 4 | 3 |\n   +---+---+---+\n   | 9 | 2 |\n 