arts:\n   - Multiplying 93 by 3 (the units digit of 83)\n   - Multiplying 93 by 80 (the tens digit of 83, which is 8 times 10)\n\n3. **Multiplying Each Part**: \n   - \\(93 \\times 3 = 279\\)\n   - \\(93 \\times 80 = 7440\\)\n\n4. **Adding the Results**: After obtaining the partial products, we add them together to get the final product:\n   - \\(279 + 7440 = 7719\\)\n\nThis method works because it leverages the distributive property of multiplication over addition, which states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). By breaking down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts, we can easily compute the final product.\n\nThe standard algorithm ensures that each digit of one number is multiplied by each digit of the other number, taking into account their place values, and then summing up all the partial products to get the final result.\n..\n</think>.",
